        "original_id": "5ebebb68-4f2b-5b24-8e73-a5b1f100488b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Heaney, Franklin D. Roosevelt\n- Organizations: Works Progress Administration\n- Places: Mount Hood, Timberline Lodge, Clackamas County, Government Camp\n- Roads: Oregon Route 173, U.S. Route 26\n- Topics: Great Depression\n\nFacts:\n- During the Great Depression in the 1930s, Charles Heaney worked as an artist for the Works Progress Administration.\n- During the Great Depression in the 1930s, Charles Heaney created several works featuring Mount Hood and Timberline Lodge.\n- Timberline Lodge was dedicated on September 28, 1937, by President Franklin D. Roosevelt.\n- Oregon Route 173 is an Oregon state highway that runs from Timberline Lodge in Clackamas County to U.S. Route 26 near Government Camp.",
